From: Toly <1397674+AnatolyRugalev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:02:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] hottyterm: HOTTY surfaces over hotty-blitz

Programs send HOTTY (HTML over the TTY) on OSC 7279; hottyterm renders
the surfaces itself through hotty-blitz's C ABI and shows each one as a
kitty image placed at the cursor. Updates are kitty frame edits (a=f,
r=1) of the damaged rectangles, the way the polyfill sends them.

All of the logic is in the new src/termio/hotty.zig. Upstream files get
hooks only, 41 lines in four files:

- Termio: the settings, osc_unknown_max_bytes, flush per read, resize
- stream_handler: the osc_unknown action (upstream #14452), full reset
- Surface: keys, clicks and hover
- GhosttyExe: link libhotty_blitz (HOTTY_BLITZ_LIB)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
